enchilada: MSS stage 6 (mss=6): GLINK over SMEM, QRTR on IPCRTR, the IPA clock query (Wi-Fi round 3)

The mss=5 modem reached ready and went fatal ~40 s later with no host services at all. mss=6 runs
stage 5 unchanged and then, instead of its 60 s watch, starts the GLINK smem edge as Linux v6.12
qcom_glink_smem.c / qcom_glink_native.c do (item 478 descriptor, 479 our 16 KiB TX FIFO, 480 the
modem's, doorbell APCS IPC bit 12, INTENT_REUSE, 8 KiB TX chunks, 16-byte FIFO reserve), accepts
only the IPCRTR channel (OPEN_ACK + OPEN as qcom_glink_create_remote; other channels are logged and
left unacked, as Linux does without a driver), runs QRTR v1 on it (apps node 1, HELLO answered as
ns.c, RESUME_TX for confirm_rx) and logs every NEW_SERVER the modem announces. It also answers the
modem's IPA clock query on the SMP2P "ipa" entry with "valid, AP IPA off" (ipa_smp2p_notify;
topaz 0113 found modem_cfg starves without it). Ported from topaz 0118/0119 with Linux's FIFO
reserve and chunking, bounded parsing of every length the modem gives, and Device-memory word
access only. "stage 6: ok" needs IPCRTR up and the modem's HELLO within 10 s; the watch runs
120 s and ends, like every failure, in the 0262 stop path. SMEM stores: items 478/479 (allocated
with the 0262 allocator, now shared with item 428) and then only our TX FIFO, the descriptor's tx
head / rx tail words and our "ipa" value. mss<=5 behave exactly as before.

